  "summary": "Internet-born music and visual language of slowed mall music, Roman busts, Windows 95 nostalgia and capitalist ennui.",
  "description": "Emerging around 2010-2011 (Chuck Person's Eccojam Vol. 1, Vektroid's Floral Shoppe), vaporwave chops and slows 80s mall pop, lounge and smooth jazz into infinite elevator serenity, paired with visuals of Greek busts, VHS grids, Windows 95 dialogs, Japanese signage and palm-tree gradients — a satire-nostalgia of consumer capitalism. Variants spun off (mallsoft, future funk, signalwave). Its palette — teal, pink, purple — is now a universal shorthand for digital nostalgia.",
